---
const items = [
  {
    q: 'Why "Lit Web Components" and not React / Vue / Svelte?',
    a: 'Lit compiles to standard Web Components, which the browser understands natively. The runtime is ~6 KB gz (vs ~50 KB for React + ReactDOM) and it does not need a build step on the consumer side. A deck stays a folder · open in 2031, it still runs.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Do I need to know Lit to write a deck?',
    a: 'No. You write HTML tags. Lit is what we used internally to build the components. The consumer surface is plain HTML and CSS custom properties · no decorators, no template literals, no class extending.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Can I print my deck to PDF?',
    a: 'Yes, via the browser. Chromium with print-backgrounds enabled gives the cleanest result. There is no dedicated CLI · slides are pure HTML, so the browser print pipeline does the job.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Is there a presenter mode with notes?',
    a: 'Yes. Wrap notes in <code>&lt;deck-notes&gt;</code> inside any slide, then press P during the talk · a popup window opens with current + next slide, the notes, a timer, and slide counter. Sync is BroadcastChannel-based; no network call.',
  },
  {
    q: 'How do I theme a deck for my brand?',
    a: 'Copy <code>themes/rikiki.css</code>, change the values, link it instead of the default. ~140 CSS custom properties, organised in two layers (palette / semantic). For a single instance, override the <code>--deck-*-*</code> tokens inline on the element.',
  },
  {
    q: 'What happens if I want a fancy animation that is not in the box?',
    a: 'You can drop a <code>&lt;script&gt;</code> inside any slide and run whatever JS you want · the slide is just an HTML host. For most needs, the four built-in transitions (slide / fade / zoom / flip) are enough; for one-off effects, GSAP and friends are a script tag away.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Why do you also pitch carousels?',
    a: 'Because <code>autoplay loop swipe</code> on <code>&lt;deck-root&gt;</code> turns the same engine into a touch-friendly carousel. Same components, same theming, same 12 KB bundle. The dual-use is a side-effect of building on web standards.',
  },
];
---

<section id="faq" class="faq">
  <div class="inner">
    <p class="eyebrow">FAQ</p>
    <h2>Common questions</h2>

    <div class="list">
      {items.map((it) => (
        <details>
          <summary>
            <span class="q">{it.q}</span>
            <span class="chev" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
          </summary>
          <div class="a" set:html={it.a}></div>
        </details>
      ))}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .faq {
    background: var(--rik-surface-raised);
    padding: var(--rik-space-7) var(--rik-space-5);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rik-border-default);
  }
  .inner { max-width: 880px; margin: 0 auto; }
  .eyebrow {
    display: inline-block;
    background: var(--rik-accent);
    color: var(--rik-accent__on);
    padding: 4px 10px;
    border-radius: var(--rik-radius-pill);
    font: 700 var(--rik-font-size-xs)/1 var(--rik-font-mono);
    letter-spacing: 0.16em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    margin-bottom: var(--rik-space-3);
  }
  h2 {
    font-family: var(--rik-font-display);
    font-size: var(--rik-font-size-mega);
    font-weight: 900;
    color: var(--rik-text-default);
    letter-spacing: -0.025em;
    line-height: 1.05;
    margin: 0 0 var(--rik-space-5);
  }
  .list { display: flex; flex-direction: column; }
  details {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rik-border-default);
    padding: var(--rik-space-3) 0;
  }
  details:last-child { border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rik-border-default); }
  summary {
    display: flex; align-items: flex-start; justify-content: space-between;
    gap: var(--rik-space-3);
    cursor: pointer;
    list-style: none;
    padding: var(--rik-space-2) 0;
    color: var(--rik-text-default);
    font-family: var(--rik-font-display);
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: -0.005em;
    line-height: 1.35;
    transition: color var(--rik-motion-fast) var(--rik-motion__ease-out);
  }
  summary::-webkit-details-marker { display: none; }
  summary:hover { color: var(--rik-accent--strong); }
  .chev {
    flex: 0 0 auto;
    width: 28px; height: 28px;
    display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center;
    border: 1px solid var(--rik-border-default);
    border-radius: 50%;
    color: var(--rik-text-default--faint);
    font: 700 1.1rem/1 var(--rik-font-mono);
    transition: transform var(--rik-motion-base) var(--rik-motion__ease-out),
                background var(--rik-motion-fast) var(--rik-motion__ease-out),
                color var(--rik-motion-fast) var(--rik-motion__ease-out);
  }
  details[open] .chev {
    transform: rotate(45deg);
    background: var(--rik-accent);
    color: var(--rik-accent__on);
    border-color: var(--rik-accent);
  }
  .a {
    padding: var(--rik-space-2) 0 var(--rik-space-2);
    color: var(--rik-text-default--muted);
    font-size: var(--rik-font-size-body);
    line-height: 1.65;
    max-width: 70ch;
  }
  .a :global(code) {
    font-family: var(--rik-font-mono);
    font-size: 0.92em;
    background: var(--rik-surface-tint);
    color: var(--rik-text-default);
    padding: 1px 6px;
    border-radius: 4px;
  }
</style>
